      ranges: [['Within ±10–15%', 'Roughly fairly priced', 'Inside normal model error'], ['Above +20–30%', 'Possibly cheap, or your assumptions are optimistic', 'Check the biggest drivers'], ['Below −20–30%', 'Possibly expensive, or assumptions are cautious', '']],
      why: 'Every model has error. A small gap is not a signal; a large gap is a reason to check your assumptions before concluding the market is wrong.',
